1
00:00:00,840 --> 00:00:04,990
<i>A skeleton dating 200 years back
found in the Himalayas,</i>

2
00:00:04,990 --> 00:00:08,440
<i>matched with the DNA
of his missing step-sister.</i>

3
00:00:08,440 --> 00:00:12,560
I want you to remember me
with those eyes of yours.

4
00:00:12,560 --> 00:00:14,130
Always.

5
00:00:14,820 --> 00:00:19,400
Kayoko Senba went to my uncle's house.

6
00:00:19,400 --> 00:00:20,490
It wouldn't be this man, is it?

7
00:00:20,490 --> 00:00:23,990
The body's all bones. No decomposing, either.

8
00:00:23,990 --> 00:00:26,590
You must be admitted to a ward.

9
00:00:34,060 --> 00:00:35,970
Wait!

10
00:00:50,720 --> 00:00:52,350
Damn it...

11
00:00:59,330 --> 00:01:01,060
[Yui Ishimizaki]

12
00:01:02,850 --> 00:01:04,150
Where are you?

13
00:01:04,150 --> 00:01:06,340
I need you here, now.

14
00:01:14,100 --> 00:01:15,790
Haruka!

15
00:01:24,130 --> 00:01:25,580
- Drive.
- Huh?

16
00:01:25,580 --> 00:01:28,920
- Just drive!
- Okay, but please don't judge!

17
00:01:33,070 --> 00:01:35,010
What happened?

18
00:01:35,010 --> 00:01:36,770
I appreciate the help.

19
00:01:36,770 --> 00:01:38,920
But you don't need to know.

20
00:01:38,920 --> 00:01:42,690
Are you a wanted man or something?

21
00:01:42,690 --> 00:01:45,060
I was set up.

22
00:01:45,060 --> 00:01:48,090
They want me admitted to a ward.

23
00:01:48,090 --> 00:01:51,550
Your father?

24
00:01:51,550 --> 00:01:54,200
That's none of your business.

25
00:01:55,190 --> 00:01:59,100
Hold on.

26
00:01:59,100 --> 00:02:05,120
Maybe your father is involved in this case.

27
00:02:05,920 --> 00:02:08,150
What?

28
00:02:08,150 --> 00:02:11,790
He was a close friend of my uncle, right?

29
00:02:12,770 --> 00:02:17,910
<i>Ishimizaki may have been involved
in some trouble.</i>

30
00:02:31,640 --> 00:02:34,010
[Kyoichi Nanase]

31
00:02:45,600 --> 00:02:50,100
It'll take a while longer
to identify the victim from this morning.

32
00:02:50,100 --> 00:02:53,870
I'm not surprised,
seeing as they were all bones.

33
00:02:54,520 --> 00:02:57,210
And the substance we found on the remains?

34
00:02:57,210 --> 00:03:02,100
It was a unique mixture of substances.

35
00:03:02,100 --> 00:03:06,310
The very same mixture that was
administered to Akihiko Ishimizaki.

36
00:03:06,310 --> 00:03:08,200
The same culprit?

37
00:03:08,200 --> 00:03:09,970
Most likely.

38
00:03:34,490 --> 00:03:36,790
Same ol' mess, huh?

39
00:03:51,780 --> 00:03:53,600
<i>What were you looking into?</i>

40
00:03:53,600 --> 00:03:55,100
<i>Nichie Pharmaceuticals.</i>

41
00:03:55,100 --> 00:03:58,910
<i>The founder was involved in some deep shit.</i>

42
00:04:05,960 --> 00:04:08,890
[Yoichi Onodera]

43
00:04:10,230 --> 00:04:12,890
Where the hell are you?

44
00:04:12,890 --> 00:04:15,630
<i>Hirama, of Toho Journal, yes?</i>

45
00:04:16,390 --> 00:04:19,200
<i>Forget everything.</i>

46
00:04:23,940 --> 00:04:25,800
Who is this?

47
00:04:26,450 --> 00:04:29,310
You're calling from Onodera's phone.

48
00:04:29,310 --> 00:04:32,580
<i>You'll find nothing in his desk.</i>

49
00:04:59,320 --> 00:05:02,620
<i>I wanted to become a real journalist.</i>

50
00:05:08,810 --> 00:05:11,230
Sir, this is Maehara.

51
00:05:11,230 --> 00:05:14,660
I don't believe he'll be
returning home today.

52
00:05:16,250 --> 00:05:17,790
Yes, sir.

53
00:05:20,460 --> 00:05:22,690
I knew it.

54
00:05:22,690 --> 00:05:28,060
Your father must have something
he doesn't want you knowing about.

55
00:05:28,060 --> 00:05:32,040
He's always on my case
when it comes to Shiharu.

56
00:05:34,820 --> 00:05:40,660
Then your sister's disappearance
and my uncle's death are somehow relevant.

57
00:05:43,980 --> 00:05:49,200
Haruka. You're still hiding
something from me, aren't you?

58
00:05:54,620 --> 00:05:58,350
Have you witnessed anyone suspicious
around these parts?

59
00:05:58,350 --> 00:05:59,980
I can't say I have.

60
00:05:59,980 --> 00:06:03,380
Then have you noticed
anything amiss recently?

61
00:06:05,060 --> 00:06:07,290
- Not really.
- I see.

62
00:06:07,290 --> 00:06:08,910
- Got it.
- May I get going?

63
00:06:08,910 --> 00:06:10,730
I have to go pick up my child.

64
00:06:10,730 --> 00:06:13,350
Of course. Thank you for your cooperation.

65
00:06:13,960 --> 00:06:14,960
What's up?

66
00:06:14,960 --> 00:06:17,100
Those bones you found.

67
00:06:17,100 --> 00:06:21,480
They were Yoichi Onodera's. I confirmed it.

68
00:06:21,480 --> 00:06:23,230
Onodera?

69
00:06:23,230 --> 00:06:26,770
Oh, that old wannabe reporter of yours.

70
00:06:26,770 --> 00:06:28,810
He was a journalist.

71
00:06:28,810 --> 00:06:31,950
Same difference. So, why was he killed?

72
00:06:31,950 --> 00:06:34,520
<i>Tell me how the investigation's going.</i>

73
00:06:34,520 --> 00:06:37,690
Share what you know, and I'll spill.

74
00:06:37,690 --> 00:06:41,230
All I can say is that they're underway.

75
00:06:41,230 --> 00:06:44,450
Then I have nothing more to tell you.

76
00:06:45,480 --> 00:06:50,220
Please keep me updated in your findings.

77
00:06:52,190 --> 00:06:54,200
Oikawa.

78
00:06:54,200 --> 00:06:55,650
How's the wife doing?

79
00:06:55,650 --> 00:06:57,240
You got a favor to ask?

80
00:06:57,240 --> 00:06:59,270
- That obvious?
- Very.

81
00:06:59,270 --> 00:07:02,980
Besides, I owe you for acting as our cupid.

82
00:07:02,980 --> 00:07:05,050
So, what did you need?

83
00:07:06,480 --> 00:07:10,090
Do you have any ties
to Nichie Pharmaceuticals?

84
00:07:10,090 --> 00:07:12,650
Nichie Pharmaceuticals?

85
00:07:12,650 --> 00:07:16,590
You write for finance.
I know you know a guy.

86
00:07:18,020 --> 00:07:21,440
He doesn't support the CEO,
if you're alright with that.

87
00:07:21,440 --> 00:07:23,400
Doesn't support him?

88
00:07:23,400 --> 00:07:25,940
[DNA match to sample "T548"]

89
00:07:27,940 --> 00:07:32,020
Is that really possible?

90
00:07:32,020 --> 00:07:36,690
Those bones were from two centuries ago.

91
00:07:36,690 --> 00:07:41,980
The STR multiplex system I utilized

92
00:07:41,980 --> 00:07:46,440
is able to pick out one individual
from a set of several hundred trillion.

93
00:07:46,440 --> 00:07:48,120
Then what?

94
00:07:49,230 --> 00:07:54,040
Are we dealing with time travel here?

95
00:07:55,850 --> 00:08:02,170
I know. He didn't believe me either.

96
00:08:04,020 --> 00:08:08,400
That's why he wants me admitted.

97
00:08:08,400 --> 00:08:10,500
Sorry.

98
00:08:16,480 --> 00:08:19,360
Thankfully, I have a change of clothes here
for overnight stays.

99
00:08:19,360 --> 00:08:23,410
Now I won't have to return home
for at least several more days.

100
00:08:25,940 --> 00:08:31,040
Do you think Shiharu passed away?

101
00:08:40,150 --> 00:08:41,960
I saw her.

102
00:08:44,850 --> 00:08:49,870
<i>I saw her during
my thesis presentation last year.</i>

103
00:08:52,960 --> 00:08:55,660
What was she like?

104
00:08:56,810 --> 00:08:58,750
I want to know more about her.

105
00:09:00,560 --> 00:09:02,410
Well...

106
00:09:06,970 --> 00:09:13,810
She was an individual who cared
for children in faraway lands.

107
00:09:15,150 --> 00:09:17,700
She cared for strangers she didn't even know.

108
00:09:20,670 --> 00:09:22,480
We're cutting your hair because...

109
00:09:22,480 --> 00:09:24,600
I'm donating it.

110
00:09:24,600 --> 00:09:30,980
Some kids are genetically born without hair.

111
00:09:30,980 --> 00:09:34,920
So people donate their hair,

112
00:09:34,920 --> 00:09:37,230
and have wigs made for those kids.

113
00:09:37,230 --> 00:09:39,270
People, like me.

114
00:09:39,270 --> 00:09:42,260
- You'll donate your hair to a stranger?
- Yeah.

115
00:09:43,440 --> 00:09:47,150
I want those kids to fight.

116
00:09:47,150 --> 00:09:48,950
Against what?

117
00:09:50,270 --> 00:09:52,160
Fate.

118
00:09:59,120 --> 00:10:00,950
You sure about this?

119
00:10:02,160 --> 00:10:04,290
Yeah. Get snipping!

120
00:10:08,540 --> 00:10:09,910
Don't move.

121
00:10:09,910 --> 00:10:11,710
Sorry.

122
00:10:11,710 --> 00:10:13,100
- Ready?
- Yup.

123
00:10:15,650 --> 00:10:21,750
<i>Shiharu and I perceived the world
in very different ways.</i>

124
00:10:23,760 --> 00:10:25,700
She saw the world with kindness in her heart.

125
00:10:35,350 --> 00:10:41,620
Someone must have tampered
with Shiharu's DNA sample.

126
00:10:42,600 --> 00:10:44,740
It was most likely swapped with another,

127
00:10:44,740 --> 00:10:49,150
by Professor Ishimizaki himself.

128
00:10:49,150 --> 00:10:51,330
Why would my uncle do such a thing?

129
00:10:54,680 --> 00:10:58,970
He may have been trying to tell me something.

130
00:10:59,810 --> 00:11:04,180
Something regarding Shiharu.

131
00:11:10,290 --> 00:11:14,650
Ishimizaki made the analysis himself.
[log.3]

132
00:11:14,650 --> 00:11:17,940
I will deal with the aftermath swiftly.

133
00:11:17,940 --> 00:11:21,520
Yes. He tampered with the sample.

134
00:11:21,520 --> 00:11:23,580
<i>There's simply no other explanation.</i>

135
00:11:34,030 --> 00:11:42,020
[The bones from two centuries ago
and his missing step-sister]

136
00:11:44,600 --> 00:11:46,580
That's Kayoko Senba.
[S]

137
00:11:48,020 --> 00:11:49,680
[Address]

138
00:11:50,910 --> 00:11:54,520
I don't think she'd speak to us again.

139
00:11:54,520 --> 00:11:57,000
<i>Do not look into it any further.</i>

140
00:11:57,900 --> 00:12:00,080
I'll search her home.

141
00:12:01,730 --> 00:12:04,150
- How?
- I'll figure something out.

142
00:12:04,150 --> 00:12:09,850
Otherwise the Professor's message
will be lost on us.

143
00:12:09,850 --> 00:12:12,790
This woman definitely knows something.

144
00:12:22,740 --> 00:12:24,560
I'll walk you home.

145
00:12:24,560 --> 00:12:26,770
No need, I'll be fine.

146
00:12:26,770 --> 00:12:31,060
Are you planning to sleep on that couch?

147
00:12:31,060 --> 00:12:34,900
Yeah, I'm used to it.

148
00:12:34,900 --> 00:12:38,690
I've practically become an insomniac
in these past few years anyway.

149
00:12:38,690 --> 00:12:43,840
I haven't managed to rest
since Mari has disappeared either.

150
00:12:44,770 --> 00:12:48,450
But let's try. We have an early day tomorrow.

151
00:12:48,450 --> 00:12:49,620
Right.

152
00:12:49,620 --> 00:12:51,440
See you in the morning.

153
00:12:51,440 --> 00:12:53,260
See you.

154
00:12:53,260 --> 00:12:54,610
[Shigeru Takagi]

155
00:12:54,610 --> 00:12:59,970
I understand you disagree
with the CEO, Mr. Takagi?

156
00:13:00,730 --> 00:13:04,810
I have nothing but complaints about him.

157
00:13:04,810 --> 00:13:10,690
Then let us eradicate
those complaints, together.

158
00:13:10,690 --> 00:13:11,920
What?

159
00:13:11,920 --> 00:13:14,320
Big fish are particularly susceptible

160
00:13:14,320 --> 00:13:19,540
to media outlets working against them.

161
00:13:20,980 --> 00:13:24,020
Kyoichi's no big fish.

162
00:13:24,020 --> 00:13:28,520
He's merely the son of the late founder,
Yumihiko Nanase.

163
00:13:28,520 --> 00:13:33,210
Kyoichi's main job
is cleaning up after his father.

164
00:13:33,210 --> 00:13:35,370
How so?

165
00:13:36,610 --> 00:13:38,360
By covering up his father's secrets.

166
00:13:38,360 --> 00:13:40,810
<i>Company image directly reflects the family.</i>

167
00:13:40,810 --> 00:13:43,020
<i>It's the downside of a family business.</i>

168
00:13:43,020 --> 00:13:46,910
<i>But if he's so desperate to save face,
Nichie is done for.</i>

169
00:13:46,910 --> 00:13:52,400
What about his father
is Kyoichi Nanase trying to hide?

170
00:13:52,400 --> 00:13:56,350
His father was practically a tyrant.

171
00:13:56,350 --> 00:14:00,040
Many were dissatisfied
with his way of management.

172
00:14:01,350 --> 00:14:04,500
Did he misuse company revenue?

173
00:14:05,400 --> 00:14:09,230
That's just one of the many
shady rumors surrounding him.

174
00:14:09,230 --> 00:14:11,510
What other rumors have you heard of?

175
00:14:13,670 --> 00:14:17,490
When it came to creating new medications,

176
00:14:17,490 --> 00:14:20,410
he supposedly did so through...
dubious clinical studies.

177
00:14:20,410 --> 00:14:23,080
Dubious studies...

178
00:14:24,790 --> 00:14:27,200
As in, human experimentation?

179
00:14:32,220 --> 00:14:34,390
That's just the rumor.

180
00:14:34,390 --> 00:14:36,840
Treat it like an urban legend, if you will.

181
00:14:37,650 --> 00:14:39,370
I see.

182
00:14:40,190 --> 00:14:44,900
But allow me to say one thing.

183
00:14:44,900 --> 00:14:50,410
From my experience,
no rumor is ever baseless.

184
00:14:51,440 --> 00:14:55,040
I won't disclose my source, so please.

185
00:15:06,280 --> 00:15:07,950
It's the Plantae.

186
00:15:09,190 --> 00:15:11,040
The Plantae?

187
00:15:12,770 --> 00:15:15,310
I can't say any more.

188
00:15:15,310 --> 00:15:18,400
- Please be on your way.
- Mr. Takagi.

189
00:15:18,400 --> 00:15:20,440
Look into the rest yourself.

190
00:15:20,440 --> 00:15:24,850
Maybe you'll find yourself mixed up

191
00:15:24,850 --> 00:15:27,020
with politicians from the MHLW.

192
00:15:27,020 --> 00:15:29,330
The Ministry of Health, Labour and Welfare?

193
00:15:33,350 --> 00:15:35,090
Thank you.

194
00:15:36,940 --> 00:15:39,040
I will be in touch.

195
00:15:53,700 --> 00:15:56,540
What are you doing here?

196
00:15:57,280 --> 00:16:01,080
I heard this is a frequent spot of yours.

197
00:16:02,270 --> 00:16:05,800
Especially when you have secrets to share.

198
00:16:06,940 --> 00:16:09,020
Did the President have you tail me?

199
00:16:09,020 --> 00:16:11,780
Is he keeping tabs on all his directors?

200
00:16:11,780 --> 00:16:18,670
No. I'm only looking into those
who are of detriment to the company.

201
00:16:20,190 --> 00:16:22,290
Know your place, boy.

202
00:16:25,200 --> 00:16:30,400
I could say the very same to you, Mr. Takagi.

203
00:16:30,400 --> 00:16:36,970
Or perhaps you're prepared
to lose that position of yours.

204
00:16:44,940 --> 00:16:48,570
This laboratory is indeed suspicious.

205
00:16:48,570 --> 00:16:52,100
They were operating without any issue,

206
00:16:52,100 --> 00:16:55,920
only to shut down without warning.

207
00:16:55,920 --> 00:17:02,020
And in the same year
as Yumihiko Nanase's passing.

208
00:17:02,020 --> 00:17:05,250
Maybe this is a potential lead.

209
00:17:10,810 --> 00:17:13,410
[Yoichi Onodera]

210
00:17:15,690 --> 00:17:19,400
Hello? Is this Onodera?

211
00:17:19,400 --> 00:17:20,950
<i>Yes.</i>

212
00:17:23,160 --> 00:17:25,560
I appreciate your offer yesterday.

213
00:17:25,560 --> 00:17:27,980
Do you remember who I am?

214
00:17:27,980 --> 00:17:29,790
<i>Yesterday?</i>

215
00:17:32,830 --> 00:17:36,690
I wish to speak about "you-know-what".

216
00:17:36,690 --> 00:17:38,410
<i>And that is?</i>

217
00:17:42,440 --> 00:17:46,730
I truly believe phones are a health risk.

218
00:17:46,730 --> 00:17:49,150
But the country acts none the wiser to it.

219
00:17:49,150 --> 00:17:51,510
Even now, wireless radiation...

220
00:19:05,270 --> 00:19:07,540
I'm sorry for the private funeral.

221
00:19:08,900 --> 00:19:13,750
I wanted to see her off with just us family.

222
00:19:15,020 --> 00:19:19,270
She was out of contact
with her other relatives.

223
00:19:19,270 --> 00:19:21,200
I'm sure this was fine.

224
00:19:30,150 --> 00:19:33,060
<i>Wrong. Try number two.</i>

225
00:19:33,060 --> 00:19:36,120
<i>Well, when you get to a hundred, wake me up.</i>

226
00:19:38,030 --> 00:19:39,990
[Dear Haruka]

227
00:19:39,990 --> 00:19:44,610
[My bones will simply return to Earth]
[I'm wishing you all the best]

228
00:19:53,880 --> 00:19:58,020
Sorry. Did you want to be alone?

229
00:19:58,020 --> 00:19:59,750
No, it's fine.

230
00:20:12,440 --> 00:20:15,420
I always reread her letters here.

231
00:20:16,350 --> 00:20:18,200
Do you, too?

232
00:20:19,520 --> 00:20:21,540
No.

233
00:20:23,940 --> 00:20:25,370
I see.

234
00:20:35,060 --> 00:20:38,160
Father says he's moving back to Tokyo.

235
00:20:39,020 --> 00:20:40,370
Yeah.

236
00:20:41,610 --> 00:20:43,890
I'm going to stay here.

237
00:20:46,210 --> 00:20:51,710
Then this might be the last movie
we ever watch together.

238
00:20:54,480 --> 00:20:56,200
We were family.

239
00:21:01,920 --> 00:21:04,390
But I guess that's over now.

240
00:21:10,980 --> 00:21:12,880
Yeah.

241
00:21:15,630 --> 00:21:18,150
There's no reason for Kyoichi to stay

242
00:21:18,150 --> 00:21:21,050
now that Mom is gone.

243
00:21:21,730 --> 00:21:24,520
He's worried about your health, too.

244
00:21:24,520 --> 00:21:26,800
I'll be fine.

245
00:21:28,540 --> 00:21:32,980
Especially thanks to this gift from Mom.

246
00:21:32,980 --> 00:21:34,590
A knife?

247
00:21:34,590 --> 00:21:36,400
Why?

248
00:21:37,280 --> 00:21:39,810
It's to protect me.

249
00:21:39,810 --> 00:21:41,260
From what?

250
00:21:48,400 --> 00:21:50,170
The monster?

251
00:21:51,980 --> 00:21:56,540
<i>A monster chased me into the mountains
when I was younger.</i>

252
00:22:22,900 --> 00:22:26,790
Let's eat breakfast together!

253
00:22:27,340 --> 00:22:29,410
- Of course.
- Keita!

254
00:22:29,410 --> 00:22:31,960
- Is that okay?
- I told you not to barge in here.

255
00:22:31,960 --> 00:22:34,190
- Can you eat natto?
- Yup!

256
00:22:34,190 --> 00:22:36,040
- I can!
- Really?

257
00:22:36,040 --> 00:22:38,080
- Yup.
- That's amazing.

258
00:22:38,080 --> 00:22:39,830
- I'm so sorry.
- What else?

259
00:22:39,830 --> 00:22:42,810
- I like eggs.
- And tomatoes?

260
00:22:42,810 --> 00:22:44,790
Tomatoes? I don't know...

261
00:22:50,650 --> 00:22:53,440
Sneaking in won't be easy.

262
00:22:53,440 --> 00:22:55,680
I'm not sneaking in.

263
00:22:56,770 --> 00:22:58,060
Oh, good.

264
00:22:58,060 --> 00:23:02,190
Then how are you getting in,
while Kayoko Senba is out?

265
00:23:02,190 --> 00:23:04,870
Kayoko Senba's husband, Kotaro,

266
00:23:04,870 --> 00:23:09,810
was a botany professor
who passed away last year.

267
00:23:09,810 --> 00:23:16,020
I'll pretend to be a former student,
and ask to pay my respects.

268
00:23:16,020 --> 00:23:20,100
I see. Makes sense to me.

269
00:23:20,100 --> 00:23:23,750
I want you to tail Kayoko Senba
when she leaves.

270
00:23:23,750 --> 00:23:26,270
With the car?

271
00:23:26,270 --> 00:23:28,120
If she takes a car, then yes.

272
00:23:28,120 --> 00:23:29,620
Aw man...

273
00:23:29,620 --> 00:23:32,080
- If it's too much...
- No.

274
00:23:32,650 --> 00:23:34,350
I'll do it.

275
00:23:34,350 --> 00:23:36,970
And you remember to smile, okay? Smile!

276
00:23:39,030 --> 00:23:43,950
So, did you bring a gift to offer the family?

277
00:23:45,900 --> 00:23:47,900
I'll go get one.

278
00:23:47,900 --> 00:23:49,960
That's the sensible thing to do.

279
00:23:52,040 --> 00:23:53,580
She's here.

280
00:23:55,580 --> 00:23:57,610
Jump!

281
00:23:57,610 --> 00:24:00,250
Nice job.

282
00:24:06,700 --> 00:24:09,000
Take care.

283
00:24:15,910 --> 00:24:18,450
[Chomei Publishing]

284
00:24:18,450 --> 00:24:20,190
[Former Minister
of Health, Labour, and Welfare]

285
00:24:20,190 --> 00:24:22,280
How was he, Hirama?

286
00:24:22,280 --> 00:24:23,980
Find anything out about Nichie?

287
00:24:23,980 --> 00:24:27,080
Yeah, he gave me a huge lead. Thanks.

288
00:24:28,560 --> 00:24:30,340
What're you looking into now?

289
00:24:36,210 --> 00:24:40,300
[Member of the Lower House, 32nd District]

290
00:24:40,300 --> 00:24:44,150
"Discussing the budget
for developing new medicines".

291
00:24:44,150 --> 00:24:48,370
[With Nichie Pharmaceutical's Kyoichi Nanase]

292
00:24:51,400 --> 00:24:53,310
Who's that?

293
00:24:54,690 --> 00:24:56,980
- Nanase?
- Yes.

294
00:24:56,980 --> 00:24:59,830
We wish to ask him something.

295
00:24:59,830 --> 00:25:01,900
I haven't seen him today.

296
00:25:01,900 --> 00:25:03,340
Shall I try calling him?

297
00:25:03,340 --> 00:25:05,980
His phone seems to be turned off.

298
00:25:05,980 --> 00:25:08,400
He's not home either.

299
00:25:08,400 --> 00:25:12,560
At the very least, he was here last night.

300
00:25:12,560 --> 00:25:16,760
His change of clothes are gone, after all.

301
00:25:17,560 --> 00:25:19,810
Is that so.

302
00:25:19,810 --> 00:25:25,010
But none of our work now
requires staying overnight.

303
00:25:25,600 --> 00:25:28,320
Since our advisor is gone and all.

304
00:25:28,320 --> 00:25:31,810
Then what was Nanase doing?

305
00:25:31,810 --> 00:25:34,410
Please don't touch that shelf.

306
00:25:35,730 --> 00:25:38,440
We keep many dangerous chemicals there.

307
00:25:38,440 --> 00:25:40,480
Such as?

308
00:25:40,480 --> 00:25:44,770
Sodium dodecyl sulfate, for example.

309
00:25:44,770 --> 00:25:46,640
A sulfate...

310
00:25:46,640 --> 00:25:49,710
It's used for extracting DNA.

311
00:25:50,650 --> 00:25:55,100
Do all students here
know how to utilize such chemicals?

312
00:25:55,100 --> 00:25:56,950
Yes.

313
00:25:58,520 --> 00:26:02,040
And the stolen skeleton...

314
00:26:04,020 --> 00:26:05,980
Yes?

315
00:26:05,980 --> 00:26:10,770
The one doing the analysis
was Haruka Nanase, correct?

316
00:26:10,770 --> 00:26:11,790
Yes, sir.

317
00:26:11,790 --> 00:26:16,500
Did you notice anything strange
about his procedures or actions?

318
00:26:17,100 --> 00:26:20,330
No, he was following all protocol.

319
00:26:25,540 --> 00:26:30,590
Haruka Nanase... He's definitely suspicious.

320
00:26:30,590 --> 00:26:34,300
He has an alibi
for when the remains were stolen.

321
00:26:34,300 --> 00:26:36,690
Does he really?

322
00:26:36,690 --> 00:26:39,690
He had easy access to those bones.

323
00:26:39,690 --> 00:26:44,200
He could've stolen them
at any other opportunity.

324
00:26:45,850 --> 00:26:48,950
Then how did he tamper with
the security tapes?

325
00:26:50,000 --> 00:26:56,620
I'm more concerned by the fact
that he's now gone missing.

326
00:26:57,230 --> 00:26:58,830
Agreed.

327
00:27:16,110 --> 00:27:18,250
- Call me if there's an emergency.
- Okay.

328
00:27:30,200 --> 00:27:35,030
[Missed Calls - Kyoichi Nanase]

329
00:27:46,650 --> 00:27:49,200
- <i>Yes?</i>
- Good afternoon.

330
00:27:49,200 --> 00:27:55,120
My name is Inoue. I studied under
Kotaro Senba at Meicho University.

331
00:27:55,120 --> 00:28:00,830
Since I was in the area,
I hoped to pay my respects to him.

332
00:28:10,150 --> 00:28:14,410
I am grateful to the Professor, and...

333
00:28:14,410 --> 00:28:16,770
<i>Please, come on in.</i>

334
00:28:16,770 --> 00:28:18,620
Thank you.

335
00:28:48,560 --> 00:28:50,380
Inoue.

336
00:28:51,450 --> 00:28:52,540
Yes?

337
00:28:52,540 --> 00:28:54,940
May I get your information in our guest book?

338
00:28:54,940 --> 00:28:55,940
Of course.

339
00:28:55,940 --> 00:28:58,240
[Takuya Inoue]

340
00:28:58,240 --> 00:29:01,790
Were you close to my father-in-law?

341
00:29:02,690 --> 00:29:04,770
Yes.

342
00:29:04,770 --> 00:29:09,770
You're quite young. He must have passed away
while you were a new student.

343
00:29:09,770 --> 00:29:12,000
He did, yes.

344
00:29:13,850 --> 00:29:15,530
I'm sorry for interrogating.

345
00:29:15,530 --> 00:29:19,830
Most who visit come for my mother-in-law.

346
00:29:19,830 --> 00:29:22,950
It's not often we get a visitor
for my father-in-law.

347
00:29:23,430 --> 00:29:26,840
The Professor, he...

348
00:29:32,070 --> 00:29:38,250
Thinking back, he took great care of me.

349
00:29:39,260 --> 00:29:41,160
I am truly grateful to him.

350
00:29:42,920 --> 00:29:45,350
I see.

351
00:29:45,350 --> 00:29:50,060
And here I thought
he only cared for his plants.

352
00:29:50,060 --> 00:29:52,520
He was a funny man.

353
00:29:52,520 --> 00:29:55,040
Pop quiz.

354
00:29:56,060 --> 00:29:58,900
What are nucleic acids always accompanied by?

355
00:29:58,900 --> 00:30:00,110
Basic proteins.

356
00:30:00,110 --> 00:30:01,510
- Wrong.
- Huh?

357
00:30:01,510 --> 00:30:05,320
- They're accompanied by nucleic 'bases'!
- What?

358
00:30:05,320 --> 00:30:11,100
He would always make
the most confusing jokes.

359
00:30:11,100 --> 00:30:15,620
Maybe fellow researchers like you
found them funny?

360
00:30:16,450 --> 00:30:19,410
We'd give him a pity laugh or two.

361
00:30:21,300 --> 00:30:23,260
Thought so.

362
00:30:24,310 --> 00:30:26,440
Haruka.

363
00:30:26,440 --> 00:30:27,900
Yes, sir?

364
00:30:27,900 --> 00:30:33,220
You don't plan on staying on
as a researcher, do you?

365
00:30:33,780 --> 00:30:36,400
- What?
- Don't worry, I take no offense.

366
00:30:36,400 --> 00:30:42,090
Just promise me
you'll continue to believe in science.

367
00:30:44,020 --> 00:30:48,160
Science is the pursuit of truth.

368
00:30:49,200 --> 00:30:51,010
It's the unveiling of secrets.

369
00:30:51,940 --> 00:30:54,790
Humans may lie, but science does not.

370
00:31:04,100 --> 00:31:07,040
You must be quite popular on campus.

371
00:31:11,160 --> 00:31:13,080
Will black tea do?

372
00:31:14,980 --> 00:31:16,540
Excuse me.

373
00:31:17,610 --> 00:31:21,190
Is Professor Kotaro's study
on the second floor?

374
00:31:21,190 --> 00:31:22,710
Pardon?

375
00:31:24,400 --> 00:31:28,310
The Professor once showed me a book

376
00:31:28,310 --> 00:31:30,730
that now appears to be out of print.

377
00:31:30,730 --> 00:31:33,560
If possible, I'd like to borrow it.

378
00:31:33,560 --> 00:31:38,200
His books are all kept
in my mother-in-law's office.

379
00:31:43,310 --> 00:31:46,170
We're technically not allowed inside
without her permission.

380
00:31:55,310 --> 00:31:59,390
I think this bookshelf contains all his books.

381
00:32:00,020 --> 00:32:01,900
Wow...

382
00:32:01,900 --> 00:32:05,270
May I take my time to look through them?

383
00:32:05,270 --> 00:32:08,770
Of course. Please stay as long as you'd like.

384
00:32:08,770 --> 00:32:13,440
Is it alright if I leave you?
I have laundry to fold...

385
00:32:13,440 --> 00:32:15,690
Of course. Go ahead.

386
00:32:15,690 --> 00:32:17,700
Thank you.

387
00:32:27,260 --> 00:32:28,690
[pass: kS9qz3m#]

388
00:33:07,900 --> 00:33:09,900
[LOCKED]

389
00:33:24,500 --> 00:33:26,260
[The aforementioned case]

390
00:33:30,330 --> 00:33:32,610
[Dr. Senba]

391
00:33:32,610 --> 00:33:38,700
[I've retrieved the bones]
[I am prepared to confront my sins]

392
00:33:40,390 --> 00:33:44,890
[Akihiko Ishimizaki]

393
00:33:44,890 --> 00:33:47,330
I knew it.

394
00:33:48,270 --> 00:33:52,600
My father had no young students.

395
00:33:52,600 --> 00:33:54,600
Shall I call the police?

396
00:33:54,600 --> 00:33:58,670
I'm sorry. I came across a term
I had to look up.

397
00:33:58,670 --> 00:33:59,950
Liar.

398
00:33:59,950 --> 00:34:02,300
You could have used your phone.

399
00:34:02,300 --> 00:34:04,350
My phone is out of battery.

400
00:34:04,350 --> 00:34:06,800
I know a liar when I see one.

401
00:34:08,310 --> 00:34:10,610
I reckon this is a fake name, too.

402
00:34:10,610 --> 00:34:13,950
I'll just call your number to be sure.

403
00:34:16,350 --> 00:34:22,620
Is Dr. Kayoko Senba really so great?

404
00:34:24,190 --> 00:34:28,190
She looks down on all those below her.

405
00:34:28,190 --> 00:34:32,010
As if those without smarts are human trash.

406
00:34:32,620 --> 00:34:37,710
A heartless person like her,
studying genetics? I can't even laugh.

407
00:34:38,700 --> 00:34:45,040
Do all researchers compete to see
who can tell the worst joke of all?

408
00:34:56,320 --> 00:34:58,950
You're honest at heart.

409
00:35:05,740 --> 00:35:09,370
What about her are you looking into?

410
00:35:11,440 --> 00:35:13,960
Is she hiding something from us?

411
00:35:14,980 --> 00:35:16,950
I can't say for sure.

412
00:35:18,100 --> 00:35:23,190
Has she done something utterly heinous?

413
00:35:23,190 --> 00:35:25,350
I wouldn't be surprised if she did.

414
00:35:33,740 --> 00:35:35,020
[Mother-in-law]

415
00:35:36,570 --> 00:35:38,310
[Yui Ishimizaki]

416
00:35:38,310 --> 00:35:40,850
Mother, what's wrong?

417
00:35:40,850 --> 00:35:43,910
<i>Haruka, you have to run.</i>

418
00:35:43,910 --> 00:35:45,240
- Huh?
- What?

419
00:35:45,240 --> 00:35:47,970
Haruka Nanase?

420
00:35:50,080 --> 00:35:52,100
Wait!

421
00:35:52,990 --> 00:35:54,300
Hey!

422
00:35:55,480 --> 00:35:57,560
Let me out!

423
00:35:57,560 --> 00:35:58,690
Please!

424
00:35:58,690 --> 00:36:00,620
My mother gave her orders.

425
00:36:00,620 --> 00:36:02,440
She said to hand you over to the police.

426
00:36:02,440 --> 00:36:04,360
Let me explain myself!

427
00:36:04,360 --> 00:36:06,850
I can't disobey my mother-in-law.

428
00:36:06,850 --> 00:36:11,300
She's a terrifying woman,
who sees through everything.

429
00:36:11,300 --> 00:36:12,740
Please, just listen to me!

430
00:36:12,740 --> 00:36:15,590
My mother has already reported you.

431
00:36:16,520 --> 00:36:20,560
I'm searching for my missing sister.

432
00:36:20,560 --> 00:36:25,000
Kayoko Senba may know something
about her disappearance.

433
00:36:25,000 --> 00:36:26,710
I apologize for lying to you,

434
00:36:26,710 --> 00:36:31,500
but I had no other leads.

435
00:36:34,910 --> 00:36:36,660
Mrs. Senba? Police.

436
00:36:36,660 --> 00:36:38,080
Are you home?

437
00:36:38,080 --> 00:36:41,370
Mrs. Senba?

438
00:36:51,770 --> 00:36:53,600
Don't.

439
00:36:53,600 --> 00:36:55,590
They'll get you.

440
00:36:55,590 --> 00:36:57,650
Mrs. Senba?

441
00:36:57,650 --> 00:37:00,690
Mrs. Senba, please answer us.

442
00:37:00,690 --> 00:37:03,600
You're investigating my mother-in-law, yes?

443
00:37:03,600 --> 00:37:05,850
Tell me anything you learn about her.

444
00:37:05,850 --> 00:37:07,410
That's all I wish to know.

445
00:37:07,410 --> 00:37:08,790
Alright.

446
00:37:09,560 --> 00:37:13,770
The number that called you early is mine.

447
00:37:13,770 --> 00:37:15,810
Promise to stay in touch, okay?

448
00:37:15,810 --> 00:37:17,500
Okay.

449
00:37:18,530 --> 00:37:22,040
Let's talk at length next time.

450
00:37:26,480 --> 00:37:29,830
Coming.

451
00:37:43,700 --> 00:37:47,120
<i>Haruka, you're safe! Thank goodness.</i>

452
00:37:47,120 --> 00:37:49,760
What about you? Everything okay?

453
00:37:51,100 --> 00:37:55,170
I'm sorry. She noticed I was tailing her.

454
00:38:09,290 --> 00:38:11,650
Please stop this.

455
00:38:11,650 --> 00:38:15,010
I already know Nanase's boy is at my place.

456
00:38:15,650 --> 00:38:18,160
I'll report him to the police.

457
00:38:18,980 --> 00:38:23,450
If I see you again, you're next.

458
00:38:26,300 --> 00:38:29,440
She knew all about our plan.

459
00:38:29,440 --> 00:38:30,410
How?

460
00:38:30,410 --> 00:38:34,410
I don't know. I'm just glad you're okay.

461
00:38:38,060 --> 00:38:41,950
I managed to find an email
Professor Ishimizaki sent to Kayoko Senba.

462
00:38:41,950 --> 00:38:44,780
<i>Really? What did it say?</i>

463
00:38:44,780 --> 00:38:47,020
"I've retrieved the bones".

464
00:38:47,020 --> 00:38:50,210
"I am prepared to confront my sins".

465
00:38:51,790 --> 00:38:53,940
Sins?

466
00:38:53,940 --> 00:38:58,060
<i>The professor committed some taboo
involving the bones from Roopkund.</i>

467
00:38:58,060 --> 00:39:00,580
But he was prepared to accept his sins.

468
00:39:01,350 --> 00:39:04,690
To face one's sins. In other words...

469
00:39:04,690 --> 00:39:07,450
He was prepared to atone?

470
00:39:08,610 --> 00:39:10,320
Exactly.

471
00:39:10,320 --> 00:39:14,020
To atone usually means to confess.

472
00:39:14,020 --> 00:39:16,480
But the Professor
was never given that chance.

473
00:39:16,480 --> 00:39:19,060
He was killed before he could.

474
00:39:19,060 --> 00:39:25,960
He sent Kayoko Senba that email
despite the risks. Why?

475
00:39:25,960 --> 00:39:28,480
I can think of two possible reasons.

476
00:39:28,480 --> 00:39:31,250
Either she was a victim, or...

477
00:39:31,980 --> 00:39:33,920
She was an accomplice.

478
00:39:36,580 --> 00:39:38,580
I'm still not sure which.

479
00:39:39,610 --> 00:39:45,180
Maybe my uncle was trying to tell you
about this sin of his.

480
00:39:49,230 --> 00:39:53,380
<i>Science is the pursuit of truth.</i>

481
00:39:54,480 --> 00:39:56,720
<i>It's the unveiling of secrets.</i>

482
00:39:56,720 --> 00:39:59,520
<i>Humans may lie, but science does not.</i>
[Shiharu Nanase]

483
00:40:00,440 --> 00:40:03,090
Shiharu is involved

484
00:40:04,270 --> 00:40:06,670
in this sin of his.

485
00:40:08,290 --> 00:40:13,830
<i>We have to find what ties the Professor
and Kayoko Senba together.</i>

486
00:40:13,830 --> 00:40:15,980
I'm right by Kanzawa Central Library.

487
00:40:15,980 --> 00:40:18,000
I'll do some digging there.

488
00:40:47,580 --> 00:40:49,220
Shiharu.

489
00:40:51,480 --> 00:40:53,010
What?

490
00:41:14,400 --> 00:41:16,000
What is it?

491
00:41:36,170 --> 00:41:37,800
I love you.

492
00:42:46,690 --> 00:42:48,170
[Darwin]
[Kayoko Senba]

493
00:43:09,790 --> 00:43:12,950
[Search]

494
00:43:20,420 --> 00:43:23,130
[ROOPKUND]

495
00:43:24,610 --> 00:43:28,270
Do you recall that nosey journalist, Onodera?

496
00:43:28,270 --> 00:43:32,270
Apparently his corpse has turned up.

497
00:43:32,270 --> 00:43:38,420
Those folks at Nichie Pharmaceuticals
may be taking drastic measures.

498
00:44:05,660 --> 00:44:08,840
Good evening, Haruka Nanase.

499
00:44:10,110 --> 00:44:11,870
I am known...

500
00:44:14,200 --> 00:44:15,950
as Ushio.

501
00:44:19,440 --> 00:44:22,080
You have gotten too involved.

502
00:44:24,740 --> 00:44:25,780
Pardon?

503
00:44:25,780 --> 00:44:29,830
You are too involved
in the mysteries surrounding Roopkund.

504
00:44:33,650 --> 00:44:35,930
I am only searching for my missing sister.

505
00:44:35,930 --> 00:44:39,310
[A Challenge to Roopkund Lake]

506
00:44:50,540 --> 00:44:52,370
Sir.

507
00:44:53,690 --> 00:44:56,620
Your visitor has arrived.

508
00:45:12,810 --> 00:45:14,950
This is...

509
00:45:19,610 --> 00:45:21,850
You...

510
00:45:21,850 --> 00:45:24,670
You killed Ishimizaki, did you not?

511
00:45:35,780 --> 00:45:39,130
Even if you managed to find your sister,

512
00:45:42,020 --> 00:45:44,790
I would simply devour her.
